  "method": "V154 tier instructions and tiers without damage. Builds reuse reviewed source-derived witnesses unchanged (paths in each 'base'). Every roll here adds a characteristic score of 2 (rollScore). The expected tier is derived from the persisted dice alone: natural roll = d10a + d10b (rule/dice/natural-roll.md); a natural 19 or 20 is always tier 3; otherwise total = natural + rollScore, tier 1 at 11 or lower, tier 2 at 12-16, tier 3 at 17 or higher (rule/dice/tier-outcome.md); a double bane lowers the tier by one to a minimum of tier 1 (rule/dice/bane.md) and a double edge raises it by one to a maximum of tier 3 (rule/dice/edge.md). damageByTier is handwritten arithmetic from the pinned ability or kit file: printed tier constants + the named characteristic score + the kit damage bonus of the chosen mode for Melee+Weapon / Ranged+Weapon abilities (chapter/kits.md Damage Bonuses), never on a kit signature, whose damage already includes its kit's bonuses (chapter/kits.md Kit Signature Ability). Instruction clauses are the printed tier clause after the damage with link markup removed; tier effects occur after the damage in printed order (rule/dice/ability-roll.md, Abilities With Damage and Effects). Forced movement, teleport, shift, Recovery and surge clauses are table instructions that change no state in V154 (docs/build/V154-tier-instructions.md). Nothing is derived from the evaluator, compiler or a run of the code under test.",
